  "live_records": {
    "q-94530": {
      "dom_id": "step-q94530",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the total charge $Q$ of a metal plate that occupies the region $D={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 2,\\,2\\le y\\le 3}$ with charge density $\\rho (x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The total charge $Q$ of a plate that occupies the region $D={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 2,\\,2\\le y\\le 3}$ with charge density $\\rho (x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{2}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{2})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-4(-\\frac{1}{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the charge of the plate is $Q=\\frac{2}{3}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
