    "q-93946": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93946",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the total charge $Q$ of a metal plate that occupies the region $D={(x,y):-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}$ with charge density $\\rho (x,y)=9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The total charge $Q$ of a plate that occupies the region $D={(x,y):-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}$ with charge density $\\rho (x,y)=9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & ={∬}_{D}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}9{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{-2}^{2}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}9{y}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{16}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}48{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}48{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =[16{y}^{3}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =16({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the charge of the plate is $Q=32.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
